From: Lukas Rieger <code@lukasrieger.com>
Subject: [PATCH] configfs: confirm unbound state after a concurrent FunctionFS close

Closing FunctionFS can unregister the gadget between configfs_write_udc's
read and disable write. The second unregistration then fails with ENODEV
even though the requested unbound state has been reached. This occurred on
Hoki while leaving ADB mode: adbd's exit stack unregistered the gadget before
usb-moded's write, causing an unnecessary charging-only fallback.

On a failed disable, confirm the current UDC is empty before treating the
operation as successful. Leave enables and still-bound/unreadable failures
unchanged. This is a postcondition check, not a retry of a failed bind.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/src/usb_moded-configfs.c
+++ b/src/usb_moded-configfs.c
@@ -749,8 +749,17 @@
         goto EXIT;
 
     if( strcmp(prev, text) ) {
-        if( !configfs_write_file(GADGET_CTRL_UDC, text) )
-            goto EXIT;
+        if( !configfs_write_file(GADGET_CTRL_UDC, text) ) {
+            /* FunctionFS close can unregister after our read. A failed
+             * disable is harmless only if its postcondition is confirmed.
+             * Never convert a failed enable into success.
+             */
+            if( *text ||
+                !configfs_read_file(GADGET_CTRL_UDC, prev, sizeof prev) ||
+                *prev )
+                goto EXIT;
+            log_debug("UDC already unbound after concurrent disable");
+        }
     }
 
     ack = true;
